1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
So far, every sum we've done has used one rod.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,900
Today, we're using two and it's easier than it sounds.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,360
Remember, each rod has its own place.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,480
The rod on the right is the ones rod.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,500
The rod next to it is the tens rod.

6
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:21,480
Together, they can show every number up to ninety-nine.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,620
Here's the whole trick for today.

8
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:27,800
We never work on two rods at the same time.

9
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:32,040
We do one rod, then the other rod.

10
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:37,460
And we always start on the right, with the ones rod.

11
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:44,120
On each rod, the lower beads move first, then the upper bead.

12
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:47,860
Each rod is just a small sum on its own.

13
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,420
Let's try twenty-one plus three.

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,840
First, make twenty-one.

15
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:57,140
Push one lower bead up on the ones rod.

16
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,680
Push two lower beads up on the tens rod.

17
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:03,460
The abacus is showing twenty-one.

18
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:05,860
Now we add three.

19
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:10,500
Three is a ones number, so only the ones rod moves.

20
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,480
Push three more lower beads up on the ones rod.

21
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,640
The tens rod doesn't move at all.

22
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,460
It's still showing twenty.

23
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:22,500
And the ones rod is showing four.

24
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,880
So twenty-one plus three is twenty-four.

25
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,180
Now let's move both rods.

26
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:32,660
Let's try thirteen plus twenty-six.

27
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:35,380
First, make thirteen.

28
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:38,760
Push three lower beads up on the ones rod.

29
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,300
Push one lower bead up on the tens rod.

30
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,980
Now we add twenty-six.

31
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,860
Twenty-six is twenty.

32
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:49,480
And six.

33
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,640
We always start with the ones rod.

34
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,800
Six is five.

35
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:56,460
And one.

36
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,520
Lower beads always move first.

37
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:01,760
So push one lower bead up.

38
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,140
Then push the upper bead down for five.

39
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,960
The ones rod is showing nine.

40
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,340
Now the tens rod.

41
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,420
Twenty means two more tens.

42
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,020
Push two more lower beads up on the tens rod.

43
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,140
The tens rod is showing three.

44
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,020
Three tens and nine ones.

45
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:27,840
So thirteen plus twenty-six is thirty-nine.

46
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,960
Did you see what we did?

47
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,780
Two little sums, one after the other.

48
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,920
That's all a big sum ever is.

49
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,360
Taking away works the same way.

50
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,040
Let's try thirty-nine take away fifteen.

51
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:49,080
Our abacus is already showing thirty-nine.

52
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,600
Fifteen is ten.

53
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,760
And five.

54
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,200
Start with the ones rod.

55
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,860
We need to take away five.

56
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,080
Five is the upper bead.

57
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:02,780
So push it back up.

58
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,040
The four lower beads stay where they are.

59
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,160
Now the tens rod.

60
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,380
Ten means one ten goes away.

61
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:15,160
Push one lower bead down on the tens rod.

62
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,100
The tens rod is showing two.

63
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:22,040
Two tens and four ones.

64
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:26,580
So thirty-nine take away fifteen is twenty-four.

65
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,860
Now it's your turn.

66
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:32,740
Make twenty-three on your own abacus.

67
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,900
Then add eleven.

68
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,420
Remember the ones rod first.

69
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:41,180
What number is showing now?

70
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,340
Twenty-three plus eleven is thirty-four.

71
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:48,440
Great job!

72
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,680
Try a few more two rod sums on your own abacus.

73
